Subject: [PATCH] DRM PRIME: cancel discontinuities and bound decoder drain

Reset is an abort, not graceful EOF: an incomplete complementary H.264
field must be discarded by flush without asking firmware to drain it.
Send a drain marker only after backpressure permits it, and only once.
Report failed input, output and drains, then abort their decoder epoch.
AddData's bool is packet consumption: consume terminally rejected input
but latch VC_ERROR for GetPicture before accepting anything else. Unlike
EAGAIN, bad input must not be retried forever. Abort releases the retained
PAFF field and stale native queues; new input still faces native reference
validation, so dependent pictures cannot reuse the failed epoch's DPB.
Hardware errors and malformed true EOF remain errors, not fake pictures.
Exported DI/renderer frames retain their existing independent ownership.

--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME.h
